Let $E_{1}, E_{2}$ and $E_{3}$ denote the events of selecting boxes A, B, C$ respectively and A$ be the event that a screw selected at random is defective. Then, $\begin{array}{l}P\left(E_{1}\right)=\frac{1}{3},P\left(E_{2}\right)=\frac{1}{3},P\left(E_{3}\right)=\frac{1}{3}\\
P\left(\frac{A}{E_{1}}\right)=\frac{1}{5},P\left(\frac{A}{E_{2}}\right)=\frac{1}{6},P\left(\frac{A}{E_{3}}\right)=\frac{1}{7}
\end{array}$ By Baye's rule, the required probability $\begin{aligned}P\left(\frac{E_{1}}{A}\right)=& \frac{P\left(E_{1}\right) P \left(\frac{A}{E_{1}}\rright)}{P\left(E_{1}\right) P \left(\frac{A}{E_{1}}\rright)+P\left(E_{2}\right)P \left(\frac{A}{E_{2}}\right)+P \left(E_{3}\right)P \left(\frac{A}{E_{3}}\right)}\\
\Rightarrow P \left(\frac{E_{1}}{A}\right)&=\frac{\frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{1}{5}}{\frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{1}{5}+\frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{1}{6}+\frac{1}{3} \cdot \frac{1}{7}}\\
&=\frac{\frac{1}{5}}{\frac{1}{5}+\frac{1}{6}+\frac{1}{7}}=\frac{42}{107}
\end{aligned}$
